        "evidence": "The condition that the printed numbers are the indicator values is supported by the proximity of the labels to the markers. The claim that screen height does not reliably rank values is supported by the 2011 data: the red marker (value 37) is higher on the screen than the blue marker (value 143), which contradicts a simple 'higher is larger' interpretation. The condition that there is no printed 2012 value is supported by observation. The conclusion that the comparison cannot be established from mark height alone is a valid inference given the 2011 contradiction.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
